SUMMARY:On the Coalgebraic Linear-Time Semantics of Two-Player Games (Ben P
 lummer)
LOCATION:LG23\, Computer Science
DESCRIPTION:Ben Plummer\nTheoretical Computer Science Seminar\n\nLinear-tim
 e semantics play an important role in program semantics and verification\,
  in settings where branching-time equivalence is too fine. Set-based coalg
 ebra provides an account of branching-time behaviour\, while finite linear
 -time semantics can be treated coalgebraically by moving to the Kleisli ca
 tegory of a monad modelling the system’s branching. In this talk\, I wil
 l discuss how these ideas extend to the linear-time semantics of two-playe
 r games. For finite behaviour\, the coalgebraic approach applies smoothly 
 to games in which the opponent’s choices are nondeterministic\, probabil
 istic\, or weighted. We characterise the resulting semantics in terms of s
 trategies that enforce…\n\nDetails: https://researchseminars.org/talk/Th
 eoryCSBham/84/
CATEGORIES:Theoretical Computer Science Seminar
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://researchseminars.org/talk/TheoryCSBham/84/
END:VEVENT
