SUMMARY:My thoughts on AI and security (Mark Ryan)
LOCATION:LG23\, Computer Science
DESCRIPTION:Mark Ryan\nTheoretical Computer Science Seminar\n\nThe first pa
 rt of my talk will be about "prompt injection"\, in which an adversary ins
 erts text in content (such as a paper\, a github README\, a CV or an email
  message) that will be processed by an LLM\, in an effort to instruct the 
 LLM to process the content the way the adversary wants. Large language mod
 els read instructions and data as one stream of tokens\, so anyone who can
  get text into that stream can potentially have it obeyed as a command. I'
 ll review real attacks\, and then compare three kinds of defence\, focussi
 ng on the type that seems to have the greatest capability to work. In a po
 ssible second part\, I'll describe a bit about how I use AI in practice\, 
 what has worked and what has…\n\nDetails: https://researchseminars.org/t
 alk/TheoryCSBham/87/
CATEGORIES:Theoretical Computer Science Seminar
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://researchseminars.org/talk/TheoryCSBham/87/
END:VEVENT
